# Tell git to stop altering line endings.  Check things out in the state they're
# saved in the repo. Modern text editors can deal with either LF or CRLF on any
# platform.
* -text

# So the bytes in a commit are the bytes on disk, and .editorconfig alone decides
# what those bytes are: LF everywhere except .bat, .cmd and .ps1, which are CRLF.
# The root .ps1 scripts drifted to LF against that rule and were converted back on
# 2026-08-26; nothing here would have stopped that, since the rule above pins
# whatever is committed rather than enforcing a convention. .editorconfig is where
# the convention lives.
